      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "I understand that well-intentioned phrases can feel dismissive when you are in this deep pain, and it is very real to feel like a core part of you is simply gone. When the pain feels this profound, it requires more than just \"self-help\" advice; it needs deep, professional support to help you navigate this loss. A therapist can help you explore this feeling of \"gone-ness\" not as an irreparable break, but as a profound need for care and understanding. Please consider that help is available to help you hold this dust while you heal.",
      "source": "target",
